# Lessons learned

Short notes about things that surprised us, so nobody repeats them. Claude reads this file at the
start of every session (it is imported by `CLAUDE.md`). Keep each lesson to a few lines.

Format:

```
## <one-line lesson>
_<date> · <who>_
What happened. **So:** what we do now.
```

---

## A broken test user looks exactly like a login bug
_starter lesson_
Stale passwords have been reported as sign-in defects. **So:** health-check test users before every run, and never report a 401 without that check.

## Screenshots lie about sizes
_starter lesson_
Measuring pixels on a screenshot undercounted sizes by about 3px and produced a wrong issue. **So:** read sizes from the design file and the live page.

## Design frame ids change
_starter lesson_
A screen was called "missing from the design" because an old frame id no longer worked. **So:** re-list the design frames every run.

## A timeout is not an outage
_starter lesson_
Every site timing out usually means the VPN or network. A 5xx error is the server. **So:** tell them apart before reporting anything.

## Bulk logins send bulk emails
_starter lesson_
Signing in dozens of test users can flood the inbox with sign-in notices. **So:** reuse logged-in sessions and warn the team before bulk runs.
